    "text": "SVP at the Hudson Square BID. Support of the DOT Canal Street redesign. Local stakeholders – businesses, residents, property owners. Improvements are critical to the neighborhood. Canal Street is a barrier to use of our businesses because the traffic congestion is so bad. Curb extension and crossings are improvements. Hoping improvements can be implemented as soon as possible. Q: (Jeannine Kiely): Does the BID support the addition of hardscape safety measures at the corner of Hudson and Canal to prevent cars from taking the turn too quickly. A: Advocated to keep the curb extension at that corner to keep cars from taking the turn too fast. The initial DOT proposal sought to eliminate that curb extension. BID is eager to support greening that area with additional planters.",
